We present a comprehensive analysis of the decay width ratios $\Gamma(B	o D\ell ar{
u})/\Gamma(B	o D^*\ell ar{
u})$ and $\Gamma(B	o d\ell ar{
u})/\Gamma(B	o s\ell ar{
u})$ within the framework of heavy quark expansion. Our findings indicate that these ratios exhibit significant deviations from their heavy quark limit predictions, with the discrepancies scaling as $1/m_Q$ and $1/m_Q$ respectively. Furthermore, we demonstrate that the $1/m_Q$ corrections are intrinsically linked to the sub-leading terms in the heavy meson symmetry multiplet.
